the idea was  scrapped under the management of the new  Warner Brothers Discovery Chief David  zazlov Matt will now change the  adaptation of the play would fit very  well into the new strategy of the  company which wants to promote more of  its in-house Brands and focus on quality  over quantity in the future as the  direct reports the film adaptation of  the stage play is being tackled by  zazlab and producers Michael Deluca and  Pam Abdi unlike the books the story is  not the work of JK Rowling directly but  of screenwriter Jack Thorne who  premiered the play in London in 2016.  nevertheless zazlab is aiming for a  strong collaboration with Harry Potter  Creator Rowling who in previous years  however has been rather averse to  adapting the play into a film her  planned involvement in the movie  adaptation is sure to attract some fans  but there is no official confirmation  yet the plot of Harry Potter and the  cursed child is about Harry and Ginny's  son Albus Severus Potter now that the  hero of the fantasy novel and movie  series is an overworked employee of the  ministry of magic his son is standing on  his own two feet and wants to follow in  his father's very big footsteps but in  doing so he puts himself in great danger  and is soon in need of help when exactly  the new Harry Potter movie is to be  released is still uncertain for now we  are waiting for official news from  Warner Brothers  when rumors started circulating some  time ago that birds of prey actress  Margot Robbie was to star in an upcoming  sixth Pirates of the Caribbean film many  fans were amazed at first glance this  was perhaps an unusual casting but as  long as the film had been a standalone  and not a cheap Jack Sparrow copy of the  opposite sex the film surely wouldn't  have performed badly in an interview  with a Vanity Fair the 32 year old spoke  about her future in the Pirates of the  Caribbean franchise and ruled out all  speculations about her role there had  been an idea for a spin-off in which she  would have played the lead role of the  interest on Disney's part seems to have  faded in the meantime so that there will  not be a collaboration after all her  clear statements in turn are creating  new rumors as to why Disney has now  backed away from the spin-off after all  due to the statements made by producer  Jerry Bruckheimer this Summer that he  and author Ted Elliott are currently  working on a script for Pirates of the  Caribbean 6. some fans now suspect that  Johnny Depp will make a comeback Depp on  the other hand has stressed several  times including trial against Amber  Heard that he will not return to Disney  thus at the moment there are no clear  answers about the future of Pirates of  the Caribbean but it could well be that  the relevant steps towards the future  will be taken in the coming months  because despite the lack of more  detailed information it does not look as  though there will be a goodbye to the  film series  there are many rumors about the upcoming  fifth Indiana Jones part especially the  return of the 80 year old Harrison Ford  who is still not quite imaginable as a  whip-wielding archaeologist is causing  some skepticism within the fan Community  up to now though there is still no first  trailer so one cannot really form an  opinion about the film yet however that  should change soon if the words of  director James Mangold are to be  believed when a fan recently asked him  when we could expect the first promo  footage mangle promised something new in  the next 30 days he didn't explicitly  mention that it would be a trailer but  given the fact that one already exists  and was shown behind closed doors at the  d23 Expo a trailer is very likely this  could also help to counter the currently  accumulating rumors that the movie is  really bad in its present form alleged  test screenings are currently taking  place where six different endings were  rated by a selected audience each is  said to have been worse than the other  with the one where Indy's goddaughter  Helena follows in his footsteps standing  out particularly badly also included was  the classic big screen death of Indiana  Jones and some sort of time travel  ending the emerging negative reports are  said to have caused some trouble behind  the scenes with Disney boss Bob chapek  internally demanding immediate reshoots  in order to still save the conclusion of  the film series director James Mangold  denies that there have been any  screenings at all which means that the  rumors should be taken with a grain of  salt for now let's first wait for the  upcoming trailer before making any  assumptions the movie is scheduled for  release on June 30th 2023  Godzilla vs Kong was certainly one of  the biggest highlights of the movie  industry last summer which had been hit  hard by the pandemic even though the  story was described as not particularly  Innovative at times there were plenty of  action sequences and many scenes that  stuck in your memory in the end in spite  of some early fighting the two giants  Godzilla and King Kong joined forces to  fight the even more dangerous  Mechagodzilla together it's all the more  fitting that the freshly revealed title  of the sequel has now been announced as  being Godzilla and Kong as for who the  upcoming villain is that the two Titans  will have to face off against well  that's still the subject of much  speculation at the moment one thing is  for sure though director Adam Wingard  wants to focus on Hollow Earth the place  of origin of Godzilla Kong and many  other Titans which is now under King  Kong's control after the last film so  far Eileen actress Rebecca Hall Bernie  actor Brian Tyree Henry and Kaylee  hoddle who embodies Gia are considered  sure returnees on the other hand it is  not entirely clear what the situation is  or regarding the two main actors Millie  Bobby Brown and Alexander Skarsgard at  least with Beauty and the Beast actor  Dan Stevens a new addition to the cast  has already been confirmed although his  exact role has not been disclosed yet  should there be any further updates on  the cast fought or the release date we  will let you know of course are you now  even more excited about the sequel  thanks to the new title and if so which  Titan do you believe could pose a real  threat to Godzilla and King Kong feel  free to post your guests in the comments  the first movie In The Chronicles of  Narnia series was released over 17 years  ago the franchise still enjoys great  popularity with the original story by  C.S Lewis being published in the 1950s  and comprising a total of seven books  three of them have already been adapted  in chronological order so there is still  enough content for at least four more  movies that is something Netflix must  have been aware of in 2018 when the  streaming service secured the movie  rights for the franchise four years  later there are now serious efforts to  also implement the films which is the  reason why there was the first news this  week following a long Hiatus according  to a report from what's on Netflix  little woman director Greta gearwig is  expected to direct not one but two The  Chronicles of Narnia movies The 39 year  old is no stranger to the film business  and is also responsible for directing  the Barbie adaptation set to debut next  year she also has several Oscar  nominations to her name so far however  due to her current involvement with the  Barbie film it will probably take some  time before where she can start work on  The Chronicles of Narnia yet her  commitment is definitely a key first  step for the production it can be  expected that they will stick close to  the books again but since the sequence  among the books is quite variable it is  impossible to say with certainty which  books gets to be adapted first anyways  we are eagerly awaiting further news  what do you guys think about gearwig's  involvement and which actors would you  love to see in the starring role let us  know in the comments down below  that's it for this week's news if you  haven't done so yet we recommend you  watch our new trailers for Puss and  Boots 2 and Magic Mike's Last Dance we  hope you enjoyed this week's Hollywood  news thanks for watching  hahaha  [Music]

